# CODEOWNERS
# Defines who reviews changes in each layer (trunk-based, mandatory review).
# Layer structure: libs/ (lowest) < packages/ < apps/ (highest)
#
# Enforcement requires branch protection on `main`:
#   - Require pull request reviews before merging (CODEOWNERS approval).
#   - Dismiss stale approvals when new commits are pushed.
#   - Require status checks to pass (build, typecheck, lint, test, layers).
#   - Block direct pushes to `main`.
#   - Require at least 2 approvals for security-sensitive paths.
#   - Restrict bypass permissions so admins cannot merge unreviewed.

# Global fallback — every file not matched below
* @casuya/maintainers @yakoboI

# Core engine (Python)
/libs/core/           @casuya/core

# Reusable frontend/TS libraries
/packages/            @casuya/frontend

# The deployable application
/apps/platform/       @casuya/platform

# Infrastructure & deployment
/infra/               @casuya/devops

# GitHub governance, CI/CD
/.github/             @casuya/devops @casuya/security
/.github/workflows/   @casuya/devops @casuya/security

# Monorepo tooling & governance
/pnpm-lock.yaml       @casuya/maintainers
/package.json         @casuya/maintainers
/pnpm-workspace.yaml  @casuya/maintainers
/turbo.json           @casuya/maintainers
/tools/               @casuya/maintainers

# Security-sensitive config
/.env*                @casuya/security @casuya/maintainers
/tsconfig*.json       @casuya/maintainers
/security/**          @casuya/security
/docs/**              @casuya/maintainers
/**/Dockerfile*       @casuya/devops @casuya/security
